<title>USA: Pioneer Rail April carloadings at new high.</title>
<headline>Pioneer Rail April carloadings at new high.</headline>
<dateline>PEORIA, Ill. 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carloadings shipped in April were the highest in the company's history, Pioneer Railcorp said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The April shipments increased by 24 percent over last year.</p>
<p>The freight shortline railroad holding company said April carloadings were 3,551 compared with 2,868 in April of last year. Carloadings shipped is one of the factors used in determining Pioneer's gross revenues, it explained.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
